From f367e3691eff32076545f6e07aa69433e1da8627 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Georgios Sokianos <walkero@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 13:25:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ftoastr: avoid clash with AmigaOS exec/types.h's FLOAT macro

Same issue as the DOUBLE clash already fixed in c-strtod.c: AmigaOS
SDK's <exec/types.h> defines FLOAT to float32, which collides with
this file's own FLOAT macro under -Werror:

lib/ftoastr.c:47: error: "FLOAT" redefined [-Werror]
---
 lib/ftoastr.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/ftoastr.c b/lib/ftoastr.c
index ef861e2237..45268c975e 100644
--- a/lib/ftoastr.c
+++ b/lib/ftoastr.c
@@ -33,6 +33,10 @@
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
+/* AmigaOS's <exec/types.h> already defines FLOAT (to float32); undef
+   it first so it doesn't clash with the one defined here. */
+#undef FLOAT
+
 #if LENGTH == 3
 # define FLOAT long double
 # define FLOAT_DIG LDBL_DIG
-- 
2.53.0

